# TODO - Owner-controlled Wi-Fi Bluetooth and AirDrop acceptance

## Required reference workflow and files

Use `.references/` at the repository root for all retained source research.
Populate it with `python3 -B tools/references/download.py`; use `--offline`
to verify existing sources. Search ignored references explicitly with
`rg --hidden --no-ignore -g '!**/.git/**' -n 'symbol|register|error' .references/`
and enumerate files with `rg --files --hidden --no-ignore .references/`.
Whenever a behavior, API or missing implementation is unclear, search these
sources and the web for the evidence needed (prefer upstream source, published
specifications and official documentation). Record exact revisions, source
hashes, adaptation scope, destinations and licenses in the single
`.references/ledger.jsonl`. Preserve upstream notices; downloaded code is not
proof of implementation or runtime success.

Concrete files for this task (paths are relative to the repository root):

- `.references/AirportItlwm-BE200/ff82f3e5647ce3885f5d48417b6356a6a23d2163/README.md` — documented native Wi-Fi setup/limitations to compare with diagnostics.
- `.references/AirPort_RTW89/90b6cfc5a69c271688fad188857cfaeb58053dc5/README.md` — documented AWDL/AirDrop limitations to distinguish from working behavior.
- `.references/ledger.jsonl` — exact source identities behind the tested commit.

## Objective

After 100% production implementation and zero-failure validation, run the
owner-authorized Dell diagnostic/repair loop alongside continuous edge-case
hardening and the remaining maintenance TODOs. The owner supplies real logs
in this conversation; agents coordinate implementation and corrections in
their chat, then repeat the CI/build/test loop.

Hardening continues indefinitely and is not an indefinite testing hold.
Source-hardening and Linux-reference retirement need not be closed to start
this loop once the implementation and validation milestones are met. Every
kernel build still requires a separately authorized GitHub `build-v*` tag.
The owner's 2026-11-10 update permits compilation even if advisory CI fails;
failures and incomplete checks must remain visible and be resolved toward
zero findings. This roadmap does not itself select or authorize a tag.

The acceptance objective is fully functional native Wi-Fi on the specified
Dell/Tahoe target, plus the requested Bluetooth/coexistence and AirDrop
behavior. Treat 100% functionality as the required outcome, never as an
unobserved result or a promise that static review proves first-run success.

