## Evidence

- Actual notebook evidence is supplied by the owner during the authorized loop.
- After authorization: owner-run device diagnostics and observed behavior.
- QCA9565/DW1707 combines Wi-Fi and Bluetooth 4.0; it does not imply a
  separate Bluetooth chipset. Qualcomm documents the combo chip and Dell
  G66T8 lists both functions and Inspiron 5567 support:
  https://www.qualcomm.com/networking-infrastructure/products/qca9565
  https://www.dell.com/support/home/en-us/drivers/driversdetails?driverid=g66t8
- Separate PCIe WLAN and USB Bluetooth HCI/firmware paths must be integrated.
  Do not infer a notebook's USB VID/PID solely from its WLAN PCI ID.
- AirDrop requires BLE plus Apple's peer-to-peer Wi-Fi/AWDL path; ordinary
  access-point connectivity does not implement that protocol. Neither a
  hardware impossibility nor successful AirDrop has been established:
  https://support.apple.com/en-ie/guide/security-pdf/sec2261183f4/web
